# CEO pack v2, Wave 2 worker phrases (#3016 step 3).
#
# One line per sheet "Words that lead here" for the 18 Wave 2 trades (T18, T19, T20, T22,
# T23, T28, T30, T31, T32, T34, T35, T36, T39, T40, T41, T42, T56, T57 in
# docs/reference/BadaBhai_Manufacturing_Taxonomy_and_Question_Pack_v2.md). Never invented.
# Hinglish rows carry "lang":"en", Devanagari "lang":"hi", pointing at the occupation
# of the trade that the phrase most exactly names (spread across each trade's bound codes
# from packages/db/data/question-packs/_families.jsonl, Wave 2 bindings).
#
# Digits are LOADABLE here (#2995 point 2, ruled 26 Nov 2026: per #3082 the validator's
# contact guard is @/URL only; T34 "ndt level 2", "asnt/isnt/pcn level 2" and T35 "iso 17025"
# are rows). 9 of 10 shorts (hbm, ndt, mpt, mpi, dpt, lpt, rac, vrf, vrv) proved 0 moves
# across the corpus and are loaded. "boe" is HELD: its L1 skeleton is "b", the same as
# greeting filler "bhai", so loading it turns every "Namaste bhai" into a bai/boe
# disambiguation and breaks the phase1 E2E gate. Held like bare plc/ppc (#3010).
#
# NOT loaded here:
#   - "gear grinding" + Devanagari twin: pinned to fam_cnc_grinding by the existing grinding
#     characterization, and the sheet says bare "grinding" asks. Held for routing.
#   - "ac ka kaam": its norm "ac" is a bare 1-token key that would move pinned "ac fitter"
#     off fam_fitter and pinned-null "ac maintenance" onto HVAC. Held for routing.
#   - "gear ka kaam" + Devanagari twin: their norms "gear"/"गियर" are bare 1-token keys that
#     would move must-not "gear oil"/"gear change" (gaadi ka kaam) onto T18 and flip the held
#     hi twin "गियर ग्राइंडिंग" off grinding. Held for routing; the gear worker still reaches
#     the trade through "gear cutting", "gear hobbing", "garari ka kaam" and the other rows.
#   - 4 sheet words that lose an exact-span tie to a production-visible published title
#     (the row would be dead weight; production would ask, not pin): "plater" (handicraft),
#     "autoclave operator" (chemical plant), "radiographer" (medical X-ray),
#     "mobile crane operator" (mobile plant).
#   - 23 same-family skips (sheet words already reaching the trade through a published title
#     or an earlier row - no duplicate row): "gear cutter", "gas cutter" + Devanagari twin,
#     "jig borer", "electroplater", "rigger" + "rigger ka kaam", "slinger",
#     "eot crane operator", "hoist operator", "boiler attendant", "boiler fireman",
#     "pump operator", "calibration technician", "calibration engineer", "ndt technician",
#     "ac technician", "ac mechanic", "ac fitting", "ac installation", Devanagari twin,
#     "kneader operator", and the 5 plating rows already on 8122.0100 ("electroplating",
#     "zinc/nickel/chrome plating" + Devanagari twin - they ride with the code into T28).
#   - 10 ka-kaam variants covered by their loaded stem (same norm): "hobbing", "honing",
#     "pipe bending", "blow molding", "ndt", "calibration" (+ Devanagari twin),
#     "fabrication", "forklift" (x2: "forklift ka kaam", "forklift wala").
#   - "boring machine operator" and "crane operator" ARE loaded (rows below) but excluded
